00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.579 align:start position:0%
European Union ministers have reached  broad agreement on priorities and ways  to share funds for the e use fishery  sector over the next seven years the  talks in brussels the ministers decided  on rules for the european maritime and  Fisheries fund a new budget created to  help fishermen adapt to the latest  reforms the epithelia verbal this is a  crucial decision for the european  fisheries sector large because the new  fund will enable us to implement the  reform of the Common Fisheries Policy  the agreement on the full general  approach will enable the presidency to  start negotiations with the European  Parliament de la paz euro rekulu a major  overhaul of the e used fisheries policy  was agreed in May the changes also  include a potentially costly obligation  to land all commercial catches and the  scientific monitoring of fish stocks the  so-called e mff funding envelope is a  key part of the reforms some of the  money could be used to fund startups for  young fisherman or to help renovate  small-scale and coastal fishing vessels  more than 35 years old the package is  aimed at bringing Europe's dwindling  supplies of fish back to sustainable  levels and providing citizens with a  safe predictable and healthy food supply  the european parliament's fisheries  committee approved its vision of the  operating rules for the EMF f which will  total more than 6 billion euros on july  10 negotiations between the council and  parliament are set to begin in autumn
 

